translated_text:
Article 9

(1) Efforts to prevent violence against women and children are carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government and coordinated by the regional apparatus organization that carries out affairs in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.

(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented by:

a. conducting guidance towards harmonious household integrity;
b. forming a working network in efforts to prevent violence;
c. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns; d. establishing a violence prevention system;
e. disseminating laws and regulations relating to the protection of women and children victims of violence; and
f. providing critical education regarding the rights of women and children to the community.

